JENKINS POLL SCM SETUP 

1.  Configure Poll SCM inside Jenkins Freestyle Job
    -   Poll SCM checks the Git repository at scheduled intervals for
        new commits.
2.  GitHub repository must be accessible from Jenkins server
    -   Jenkins requires internet access to poll GitHub.
3.  Open Jenkins → New Item → Freestyle Project
    -   Creates a new Jenkins job for SCM polling.
4.  Under Source Code Management select Git
    -   Enables Git repository integration.
5.  Repository URL:
    https://github.com/Sudarsanaa-Mathan/nginx-node-alpine-docker-app.git
    -   Specifies the GitHub repository to monitor.
6.  Branches to build: */main
    -   Configures Jenkins to monitor the main branch.
7.  GitHub → Settings → Developer Settings → Personal Access Tokens →
    Fine-grained tokens
    -   Opens token generation section.
8.  Click Generate new token
    -   Starts token creation process.
9.  Select Repository access → Only select repositories → Choose
    nginx-node-alpine-docker-app
    -   Grants access only to required repository.
10. Under Repository permissions enable Contents: Read-only
    -   Allows Jenkins to clone repository.
11. Click Generate token and copy it immediately
    -   Token is shown only once and used as Jenkins password.
12. Click Add under Credentials → Select Username with password
    -   Creates HTTPS authentication credential.
13. Username: Sudarsanaa-Mathan
    -   Enter your GitHub username.
14. Password:
    -   Paste generated GitHub token instead of password.
15. Click Add and select the credential
    -   Saves and activates authentication for repository access.
16. Scroll to Build Triggers and select Poll SCM
    -   Enables periodic repository checking.
17. H/5 * * * *
    -   Polls repository every 5 minutes for changes.
18. Click Save
    -   Stores job configuration.
19. Go to GitHub → nginx-node-alpine-docker-app → index.html → Click
    Edit
    -   Opens file for modification.
20. Add:
    Poll SCM Test
    -   Inserts a visible change to trigger polling.
21. Click Commit changes
    -   Creates a new commit in the repository.
22. Wait up to 5 minutes
    -   Jenkins automatically checks for new commits.
23. Jenkins → Job → Build History
    -   Displays automatically triggered build.
24. Open Console Output and verify ‘Started by an SCM change’
    -   Confirms build was triggered by Poll SCM.
25. git –version
    -   Verifies Git is installed on Jenkins server.
26. ping github.com
    -   Confirms Jenkins server has internet connectivity to GitHub.
